# Evolve (CR 702.100a, 603.4): two creatures enter together (Lingering Souls' two 1/1 Spirits), so Cloudfin Raptor (0/1)
# triggers twice, each time because a Spirit has greater power. The first resolves and the Raptor is 1/2; as the second tries
# to resolve the intervening "if" is checked again: neither the power (1) nor the toughness (1) of the Spirit beats 1/2, so it
# does nothing (the ruling's own example). The Raptor ends with one counter, not two. Black Lotus (three white) pays for
# Lingering Souls and Mox Sapphire for the Raptor.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Sapphire
Cloudfin Raptor
Lingering Souls
Island x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Island x20

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Cloudfin Raptor.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Hand.Lingering Souls.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Triggers(Evolve; Evolve)
? Stack.Count = 2
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudfin Raptor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Stack.Count = 0
[T1 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudfin Raptor.Counters.PlusOnePlusOne = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudfin Raptor.Power = 1
Bot1.Battlefield.Cloudfin Raptor.Toughness = 2
